<title>CANADA: Quebec to force salary disclosure of ME-listed cos.</title>
<headline>Quebec to force salary disclosure of ME-listed cos.</headline>
<dateline>QUEBEC CITY 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Quebec National Assembly adopted legislation on Tuesday to require companies traded on the Montreal Exchange to disclose the remuneration of their five top executives.</p>
<p>The bill will force companies to detail salaries, benefits, bonuses and stock options of such officials.</p>
<p>This follows the lead of the Ontario Securities Commission and U.S. regulators.</p>
<p>	 ((Reuters Quebec City Bureau:418-648-6442))</p>
